    "recommendations": "Reducing brush and dense shrub cover adjacent to the structure and within the immediate structure perimeter could meaningfully improve defensible space and reduce fuel continuity near improvements. Creating and maintaining separation between shrubs, mixed vegetation, and the structure itself may reduce structure exposure and support suppression operations should fire approach the property. Where shrubs are scattered across open terrain, managing spacing between individual plants could reduce opportunities for fire to spread continuously across the parcel. The long driveway and vegetated access route represent an important consideration for firefighter access and evacuation; managing vegetation along both sides of the driveway to maintain clearance overhead and at the margins would support emergency vehicle movement and reduce fuel continuity along that corridor. Sustaining these vegetation management efforts over time, particularly within the areas closest to the structure and along the primary access route, could improve overall wildfire resilience and property preparedness at this wildland interface location."
